From c03a443646e4db28eefc93b1a97b4c82c81e62e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <dsh@nord.local>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: add opt-in read-only ufsd probe

Vendor crates/ufs from the redox-oneplus6 repo as drivers/ufs-core and
add drivers/ufsd: a one-shot probe that starts only when the kernel
device tree declares qcom,sdm845-ufshc, brings the link up read-only
(HCE cycle, DME link startup, NOP, fDeviceInit, LU enumeration, READ
CAPACITY, one READ(10) of LBA 0..33) and prints the CRC-checked GPT
header and ESP entry. The command builder is closed over the SCSI
allowlist; no WRITE-class opcode can reach the bus (host tests in
drivers/ufs-core).

On the qemu-oneplus6 emulator QCOM vendor DME attributes are not
modelled, so ufsd logs the MPHY_TX_FSM_STATE gap and retries without
the vendor register path.

Wire it into the ramboot-initfs profile only (RAMBOOT_BINS,
30_ufsd.service, 90_ramboot.target); other profiles are unchanged.

Agent: DeepSeek Harness
Model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (5090 lane)
Provider: Qwen
Refs: EMU-UFS-RO
